1. Converse's RUN_ERROR carries rawEvent (toRunErrorRawEvent), as the other
   adapters' do since TanStack/ai#985; it had none, so the provider status
   was lost. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
2. A Converse stream that ends without messageStop throws (code
   incomplete-stream), so chatStream reports a RUN_ERROR instead of finishing
   the cut-off answer as stop. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.
3. The terminal event carries messageStop's stopReason (null when it has
   none) as
   metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every stop reason from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead
   of reading an unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the
   raw reason.

